<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Legio III Augusta</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Third Legion Augusta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Legio III Augusta was a Roman legion stationed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> from the reign of Augustus into the 5th century. Based first at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ammaedara">Ammaedara</a>, then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tebessa">Theveste</a> and from the 120s at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lambaesis">Lambaesis</a> in Numidia, it guarded the frontier and built roads and towns. Disbanded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gordian-iii">Gordian III</a> in 238 for its part in the fall of the Gordians, it was re-formed in 253.</p></div>
